    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "It sits at the junction of state routes 130 and 981, 6.3 miles southeast of Greensburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasant_Unity%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Jamison Coal and Coke Company ran an underground bituminous coal mine near Pleasant Unity from 1918 to the early 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasant_Unity%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The mine’s company store was on Route 981 at Phillips Street in Pleasant Unity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasant_Unity%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By 1940, the mine employed about 300 miners, making it a major local employer.",
